{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1001", "sample_idx": 37, "model_name": "stockmark/stockmark-2-100b-instruct", "content": "Fair traveller, ere thou dost embark on thy journey to the land of the rising sun, let me weave for thee a tapestry of days, a Shakespearean itinerary, where each moment doth unfold in grandeur and style.\n\nDay one, thy feet shall tread upon the sacred earth of Tokyo, where the neon lights dance like fairies in the night, and the ancient temples stand as sentinels of time. Begin thy day at the Meiji Shrine, where the whispering pines and the scent of incense shall guide thy spirit. Then, wander through the bustling streets of Harajuku, where the youth doth express their souls in vibrant attire and the cafes doth offer sweet respite.\n\nDay two, thy journey doth lead thee to Kyoto, the city of a thousand temples. Ascend the steps of Kiyomizu-dera, where the wooden stage doth overlook the city, and the cherry blossoms in spring shall paint the landscape in hues of pink. In the evening, stroll through the Gion district, where the geisha doth move with grace, and the traditional tea houses doth beckon thee with promises of refinement.\n\nDay three, let the mountain air of Nikko refresh thy senses. Here, the Toshogu Shrine doth stand as a monument to the Shogun, and the surrounding forests doth murmur tales of the past. In the afternoon, take a dip in the soothing hot springs of Kinugawa, where the waters shall wash away the worries of the day.\n\nDay four, thy heart shall find solace in the beauty of Hiroshima. Begin at the Peace Memorial Park, where the message of hope doth resonate in the silence. Then, cross the Seto Inland Sea to the island of Miyajima, where the torii gate doth greet thee with its timeless beauty, and the deer doth roam free.\n\nFinally, on day five, return to Tokyo, where thy journey doth culminate in a feast for the senses. Visit the Tsukiji Outer Market, where the freshest of seafood and the vibrant energy doth fill the 